.TH plocate-showdiff 1 "Nov 2025" plocate

.SH NAME
plocate-showdiff \- compare plocate databases or history logs

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B plocate-showdiff
.RI [ --history ]
.I PLOCATE_DB
.br
.B plocate-showdiff
.I OLD_DB NEW_DB
.br
.B plocate-showdiff
.RI --live " ROOT " PLOCATE_DB

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B plocate-showdiff
inspects the metadata that
.BR updatedb (8)
stores inside a plocate database. It can replay the internal history log,
diff two database snapshots, or compare a database against a live filesystem
root (recomputing metadata and optional hashes).

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --history
Print the recorded add/remove/modify events stored alongside
.I PLOCATE_DB .
The log is ordered chronologically; run markers are automatically skipped in
the output.

.TP
.I OLD_DB NEW_DB
When invoked with two database paths,
.B plocate-showdiff
compares their metadata and prints one line per change (ADDED/REMOVED/MODIFIED)
including the old and/or new attributes.

.TP
.BI --live " ROOT"
Diff a database against the live filesystem rooted at
.IR ROOT .
Every database entry is stat(2)'d, hashes are recomputed when they were present
in the database, and new files under
.I ROOT
are reported as additions. This mode is useful for verifying backups or forensic
snapshots.

.TP
.B --help
Show a short usage summary.

.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success and non-zero on errors (corrupt database, I/O failure,
or command-line usage errors).

.SH FILES
.TP
.I @dbfile@
Default plocate database (as consumed by the history mode).

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR plocate (1),
.BR updatedb (8),
.BR plocate-build (8)
